/-!
# Atlas V-03 (block D, part 2): the eight frozen III residuals `res1a … res1d`, `res1aN … res1dN`

Each complexified, source-free linearised NP identity (`V03C3`) is evaluated on single-mode fields: frame derivatives
of mode fields are III's `j = 0` operators (V-01 `mode_directions`), the prefactors `q, q̄` of the scaled fields are
differentiated by the 2D product rule (`cpd_pref`), and the KN spin coefficients are inserted (V-02 tables; the
`B`-suffixed ones in `npKN_B`). The `j` terms, `3/ρ̄*` and `3ia sin θ/ρ̄*` of III come out of these derivatives
and coefficients; III's definitions are imported unchanged. Only `phaseP`, `q`, `q̄`, `√2`, `Σ`, `Δ`, `sin θ`
(proved nonzero on `domKN`) and, in `res1d`/`res1dN` only, `Q` (`p.hQ : Q ≠ 0`) are divided by; never `ω`, `m`, `F₊`, `F₋`. -/

